  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to Amazon Bioeconomy and Forest Management Multi-Donor Fund (MDTF) under the Amazon Initiative of the Inter-American Development Bank.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Amazon Bioeconomy and Forest Management Multi-Donor Fund (MDTF) will be an anchor donor fund of the IDB&#x2019;s Amazon Initiative. As such, the MDTF aims to support the Amazon Initiative&#x2019;s objective to foster socio-environmentally sustainable and inclusive economic development models in the Amazon region that benefit its diverse communities, especially through the thematic areas of Sustainable Agriculture, Livestock and Forest Management and Bioeconomy, as well as via the deep integration of the Initiative&#x2019;s three transversal issues (forest conservation; gender and diversity; institutional strengthening) throughout the portfolio of investment projects, technical cooperation and enabling activities carried out under the Initiative. The MDTF will focus specifically on supporting eligible operations in the three primary lines of action: 1) support to resilient, diverse landscapes; 2) promotion of Amazon-positive value chains; and 3) sustainability in commodity supply chains. Operations under the MDTF will contribute to the conservation and restoration of forested landscapes, and improved resilience and livelihoods of local communities.</narrative>
  </description>
